  "question": {
    "text": "A common tangent to the conics $x^2=6 y$ and $2 x^2-4 y^2=9$ is:",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "WZkih",
      "text": "\n$x-y=\\frac{3}{2}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "oOOJO",
      "text": "\n$x+y=1$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GGbPW",
      "text": "\n $x+y=\\frac{9}{2}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ZhASw",
      "text": "\n$x-y=1$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&x^2-6 y \\\\\n&2 x^2-4 y^2=9\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nConsider the line,\n$$\nx-y=\\frac{3}{2}\n$$\nOn solving (i) and (iii), we get only\n$$\nx=3, y=\\frac{3}{2}\n$$\nHence $\\left(3, \\frac{3}{2}\\right)$ is the point of contact of conic (i), and line (iii)\nOn solving (ii) and (iii), we get only $x=3$,\n$$\ny=\\frac{3}{2}\n$$\nHence $\\left(3, \\frac{3}{2}\\right)$ is also the point of contact of conic (ii) and line (iii).\nHence line (iii) is the common tangent to both the given conics.",
    "image": null
  },
